From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: John Vishnefske <jvishnefske@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 18:09:31 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] std: unwinding and backtraces on linux-none with the
 unwinding crate

There is no libgcc_s or libunwind to link, so the unwind crate uses the
pure-Rust `unwinding` crate there, as Xous does (features unwinder,
fde-custom, dwarf-expr; core only). Its exception header reserves six
words on x86_64, so _Unwind_Exception does too.

sys/pal/linux_none registers the FDE finder at init: the executable's
.eh_frame_hdr, located by PT_GNU_EH_FRAME in the program headers from
AT_PHDR (linux_none_rt::elf). Unwinding works with -Cpanic=unwind, and
_Unwind_Backtrace under either strategy.

backtrace-rs's gimli symbolizer gets a linux-none mmap (through
linux_none_rt) and a native_libraries that reports the executable from
the same program headers, in place of libc's mmap and dl_iterate_phdr.
